    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.animate\n\n### Description\n\nIf I paste from the OS using Cmd-V in iTerm2 while mini.animate is enabled, and the amount of text being pasted causes the screen to scroll part way through, mini.animate moves the cursor during the paste and causes the text to become scrambled.\r\n\r\nWorkaround is to \"zt\" and paste a small amount of text at a time or to disable mini.animate before pasting.\r\n\r\nI also attempted the proposed workaround in #275, but like the original poster there, I got an error: Lua Diagnostics.: Duplicate field `paste`, and it didn't help. Using `\"+p` does work, though.\r\n\r\nWould be nice if mini.animate could tie into a system paste (neovim can detect this, since you don't have to be in insert mode to paste text with Cmd-V, so hopefully it also exposes it somehow) and temporarily disable animation for the duration of the paste.\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.9.5\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. `nvim -nu minimal.lua`\r\n\r\n```lua\r\n-- Fix the janky mouse scrolling with mini.animate\r\nlocal anim_loaded, animate = pcall(require, 'mini.animate')\r\nif anim_loaded then\r\n  local scrolled = false\r\n  for _, scroll in ipairs({ 'Up', 'Down' }) do\r\n    local key = '<ScrollWheel' .. scroll .. '>'\r\n    vim.keymap.set('', key, function()\r\n      scrolled = true\r\n      return key\r\n    end, { noremap = true, expr = true })\r\n  end\r\n\r\n  vim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('WinScrolled', {\r\n    callback = function()\r\n      vim.schedule(function()\r\n        scrolled = false\r\n      end)\r\n    end,\r\n  })\r\n\r\n  animate.setup({\r\n    scroll = {\r\n      enabled = false,\r\n      timing = animate.gen_timing.linear({ duration = 150, unit = 'total' }),\r\n      subscroll = animate.gen_subscroll.equal({\r\n        predicate = function(total_scroll)\r\n          if scrolled then\r\n            return false\r\n          end\r\n          return total_scroll > 1\r\n        end,\r\n      }),\r\n    },\r\n  })\r\nend\r\n```\r\n\r\n2. Copy a large amount of text into the system clipboard.\r\n3. Paste into neovim.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nShould paste the desired text.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nMoves the cursor midway through paste, jumbling the text.",
