            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "One additional note: while trying to get a screen recording for this, I was playing around a bit with the paste settings to make it a little easier to see what is going on. When I paste super slowly, it can take forever to paste, but also, mini.animate can move the cursor rapidly enough between chunks that the paste generally works. And I also found the opposite to be true, with a fast enough paste, apparently iterm can actually send all the data before mini.animate has a chance to react, so moderate sized pasting can succeed.\r\n\r\nHowever, in those in-between speeds, especially speeds that are likely to be in play during ssh sessions, mini.animate moves the cursor and messes up the paste.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/6116062/e30d6261-56d3-482a-ba39-7c04a4970ccd\r\n\r\n",
